1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,378
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:07,716
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:10,885
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:13,012
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:17,934
How was your date with Cathy?

7
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:18,893
We're together now!

8
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:20,562
What? You thought I got rejected?

9
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:22,605
This wouldn't have happened without you.

10
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:23,565
[Cathy] Gavsy!

11
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:26,443
Can you take a video of me
while I donate blood?

12
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:27,527
[Gavin] <i>Sure, let's go.</i>

13
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:30,947
Let's eat at the lechon restaurant
at the mall.

14
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:31,906
[Tonet] <i>That's Audrey's, huh.</i>

15
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,576
Ah, sir! Can we follow that car?

16
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:39,164
Where's the man who caught the thief
who stole my phone yesterday?

17
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:41,374
- That was me.
- [Denden] <i>It wasn't you.</i>

18
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,126
<i>It was the handsome curly-haired guy.</i>

19
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:46,546
I saw that <i>Wonderkids</i> is showing now!
What do you think?

20
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:49,090
- G! I want that--
- I actually like that more.

21
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:50,717
Let's buy tickets.
We don't have tickets yet!

22
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,427
- [Atoy] Looks like it's starting.
- [Tonet] <i>Is Audrey here?</i>

23
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:53,636
I'll knock on her door.

24
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:54,929
Uh, what does she want?

25
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:57,807
[in English] Are you saying that Janine
is not really their child?

26
00:00:57,891 --> 00:01:01,061
Let's retest to be sure.

27
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:03,938
She doesn't need to do that,
and she doesn't need to listen to you.

28
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:05,482
[in English] Please, just leave.

29
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,817
Why don't you want me to talk to Audrey?

30
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:08,943
PREVIOUSLY

31
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:09,944
Are you hiding something?

32
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:11,571
Audrey, Audrey!

33
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:12,947
- [Red] <i>Hey!</i>
- [Tonet gasps]

34
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:14,032
[Red] <i>Why are you pushing my wife, huh?</i>

35
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:15,158
What's your problem? Who are you?

36
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:16,409
You're a trespasser, aren't you?

37
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:19,037
- Do you want me to kill you?
- [Tonet] <i>Whoa! I'm leaving!</i>

38
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,039
Make sure your boys follow that woman.

39
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:22,665
Don't let her get close to Atoy.

40
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:24,501
[Mongki] <i>What's our plan for her, boss?</i>

41
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:26,002
We'll exploit her.

42
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:28,713
If she resists…

43
00:01:29,756 --> 00:01:30,882
you know what to do.

44
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:37,180
[music fades]

45
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:38,848
- Daddy, let's run.
- We'll be late…

46
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:40,767
Oh, I'll get it. I'll come back for you.

47
00:01:43,978 --> 00:01:45,814
[suspicious music playing]

48
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:47,649
Ibyang, your shoelace!

49
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:49,526
Fix it, quick!

50
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:50,527
[Ibyang grunts]

51
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:51,736
There.

52
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,998
[music fades]

53
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:10,547
[tense music playing]

54
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,136
Where are they?

55
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:24,435
[suave theme music playing]

56
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:25,854
[motorcycle revving]

57
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:26,813
[sewing machine whirring]

58
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:27,772
[scratches]

59
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:28,731
[snipping]

60
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,235
[sewing machine clacking]

61
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:34,904
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

62
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:37,031
[gunshots]

63
00:02:37,115 --> 00:02:39,325
[clicking]

64
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:40,743
[snipping]

65
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:47,125
[electronic blipping]

66
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:54,549
- [pensive music playing]
- [old woman] <i>Your misfortune</i>

67
00:02:54,632 --> 00:02:56,926
<i>will come in threes!</i>

68
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:01,598
If not you, then maybe

69
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:05,101
the one you love.

70
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,397
[phone blips]

71
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:16,446
Hello, Tonet?

72
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:19,657
Oh, brother? Oh,
I'm on my way to the mall.

73
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,951
Seems you've been on your way for a while.

74
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:26,122
Uh, maybe… you should just go home first?

75
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:27,999
So… it's safe.

76
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:30,251
I'm already on my way. It's fine, brother.

77
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:33,546
I'm on my way.
Let's just chat at the restaurant.

78
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:36,758
And I have a lot to tell you.

79
00:03:36,841 --> 00:03:39,302
[Tonet] <i>I don't have anyone to talk to.</i>

80
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:40,762
<i>I can't tell Atoy.</i>

81
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:42,138
What's it about?

82
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:44,390
Okay, okay. Let's just meet
at the restaurant.

83
00:03:44,474 --> 00:03:46,226
Yes, okay.

84
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:47,352
No problem, love--

85
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:48,436
[line beeping]

86
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:49,437
Hello?

87
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,522
- Tonet. Hello?
- [line beeping]

88
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:53,066
[tense music playing]

89
00:03:53,149 --> 00:03:54,984
Sir, sir, do you have a charger?

90
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,611
[driver] I don't, ma'am.

91
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:58,947
[softly] I'm giving you one star.

92
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:03,243
[music swells]

93
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:06,746
[music fades]

94
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:14,379
Oh, where's Ibyang?

95
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:17,799
Um, Ibyang? I don't know.

96
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:20,093
- She was just behind me earlier.
- [indistinct]

97
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:22,804
What do you mean you don't know?
Where did she go?

98
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:25,223
- Um…
- [Atoy] Huh?

99
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:26,641
[suspicious music playing]

100
00:04:26,724 --> 00:04:28,726
You were just together earlier.
Where's Ibyang?

101
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:31,479
[stammering]

102
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:32,814
Miss, uh…

103
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:34,816
Uh, cancel.

104
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:36,359
- We're not going to watch the movie.
- Wait--

105
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:38,569
I thought we're going to watch a movie?

106
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:40,655
How can we,
if you don't know where Ibyang is?

107
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:41,614
We'll look for her.

108
00:04:42,573 --> 00:04:44,909
Miss, sorry, but we'll just try
to come back.

109
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:47,078
Uh, Daddy, maybe we should
go to the first floor.

110
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:48,288
Maybe she stayed there.

111
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:49,831
- [in English] First floor?
- First floor…

112
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:51,124
- [Janine] Yes.
- [Atoy] Come on…

113
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:54,961
[music fades]

114
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:56,462
BE A HERO
DONATE BLOOD TODAY

115
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,015
[T-Bak chuckles]

116
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:08,182
- Hey.
- [quirky sting]

117
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:13,604
Karla, let's play basketball later.
Let's bet on it!

118
00:05:14,188 --> 00:05:15,315
You guys go ahead.

119
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,900
Oh? Why do you look so down?

120
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,695
Did they take a lot of blood
from you earlier?

121
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:21,946
‪[quirky sting]

122
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:26,784
You know, the cure
for your blood loss is here! [chuckles]

123
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:30,246
- Huh?
- [both] Gavin!

124
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,331
[elated sound]

125
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:33,082
- [giggles]
- [stammers]

126
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,584
Stop it already.

127
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:37,295
He's with Cathy now. Let them be together.

128
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:38,671
- Huh?
- What?

129
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,632
- Jealous.
- What do you mean?

130
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:44,177
[pensive music playing]

131
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:46,554
Uh, together.

132
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:49,807
Through thick and thin.

133
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:53,186
[chuckles] Karla, we're not
getting married yet.

134
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:56,022
But you know what?

135
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:57,607
[in English] I really need to thank you.

136
00:05:58,191 --> 00:06:01,569
You convinced me
to give Gavin a second chance.

137
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:04,864
He's so fun to be with, right?

138
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:07,867
And so humble, just like you said.

139
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:11,913
So, I said yes to him!

140
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:13,581
[T-Bak] What?

141
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:15,708
You're Gavin's girlfriend?

142
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,085
[both] Really?

143
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:21,047
[in English] Karla, here's the thing.

144
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:25,885
I know you're close to Gavsy, my babe.

145
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:28,638
But since we're together now,

146
00:06:28,721 --> 00:06:32,016
I wouldn't really feel
too comfortable with him getting

147
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,102
too close to other girls.

148
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:37,355
[in English] And that includes you.

149
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:39,273
[in English] So, I hope you understand.

150
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:42,068
They're just friends.

151
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:43,569
And also, she--

152
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:45,696
So arrogant.

153
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:47,448
[in English] Okay.

154
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,450
That's not a problem.

155
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:51,410
[in English] Okay, thanks. Bye!

156
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:53,204
[melancholic music playing]

157
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:54,497
She's so fussy.

158
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:56,707
[T-Bak] Acting like she's special.

159
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:07,093
[ominous music playing]

160
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:31,826
- [line ringing]
- [tense music playing]

161
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:32,743
Boss.

162
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:35,997
Roger, Mongki said you're here.

163
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,582
We're at Terrazza Mall.

164
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,709
Looks like she's meeting someone here.

165
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,295
[Red] <i>We're here too.</i>

166
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:45,339
Boss,

167
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:48,301
the picture you showed me, Atoy

168
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:49,552
and your niece are here.

169
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:51,053
Don't show yourself to them.

170
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:53,139
But make sure

171
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:55,099
Tonet doesn't see them.

172
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:57,977
[man] What?

173
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:04,817
Where is she?

174
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:09,739
Um… Daddy, where are we going?

175
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:12,617
The administration office.
Let's ask for help.

176
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,785
So they can help us look for Ibyang.

177
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:19,081
Um, Daddy, I'll just go to the CR first.

178
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,958
[pensive music playing]

179
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:22,668
All right, all right. I'll wait for you.

180
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:26,297
[tense music playing]

181
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:39,560
- [music fades]
- [inaudible]

182
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:45,900
♪ <i>Don't get ahead</i> ♪

183
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:47,693
♪ <i>Of the feelings</i> ♪

184
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:51,614
♪ <i>Of my heart</i> ♪

185
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:56,536
♪ <i>That's no stranger to this…</i> ♪

186
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,538
Karla, are you okay?

187
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:00,957
I'm fine.

188
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:05,002
["Sa Wala" by Wickermoss
with Weth Macam playing]

189
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:07,713
You know, you don't have to pretend.

190
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:12,468
If you're not okay, then you're not.

191
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:18,724
If you don't want to share yet,
I won't force you.

192
00:09:19,225 --> 00:09:22,687
♪ <i>Not that</i> ♪

193
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:28,025
♪ <i>I'm thinking badly</i> ♪

194
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:30,528
♪ <i>There are many like you…</i> ♪

195
00:09:30,611 --> 00:09:32,280
But can I hug you?

196
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:36,576
♪ <i>What has passed and carried</i> ♪

197
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,828
♪ <i>Hard to let go</i> ♪

198
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:42,331
♪ <i>Hard to let go</i> ♪

199
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:48,045
♪ <i>I don't want games…</i> ♪

200
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:51,632
I think I know why you're crying.

201
00:09:52,466 --> 00:09:53,843
It's Gavin, isn't it?

202
00:09:55,511 --> 00:09:59,557
Sis Ame, he's with Cathy now.

203
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:01,851
What?

204
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:05,813
He beat Tonet and me
in having a relationship.

205
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:09,400
Too bad Tonet isn't here.

206
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:14,822
Then both of us could give you
advice as your sisters.

207
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:19,118
I've been texting her nonstop.
She's not replying.

208
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:21,370
Where is she?

209
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:24,332
Well, she was looking for Atoy.

210
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:26,250
Maybe they're together now.

211
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:35,468
♪ <i>Forcing us to have something together</i> ♪

212
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:41,140
♪ <i>If it's only for nothing…</i> ♪

213
00:10:41,223 --> 00:10:42,516
Let it go.

214
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,310
[music fades]

215
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:55,613
[ominous music playing]

216
00:10:57,573 --> 00:10:59,033
Mmm, Janine!

217
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:01,827
You're with Atoy?

218
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:02,995
[Janine] No.

219
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:04,830
Then who are you with?

220
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,374
None of your business.

221
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:08,167
Janine!

222
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:09,960
- [tense music playing]
- [Tonet] Oh.

223
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:12,380
Oh, sorry--

224
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:14,173
Oh, my. Sorry.

225
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:15,800
Sorry, sorry.

226
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:18,052
[woman] Where are you even going?

227
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:19,720
[in English] You're so careless!

228
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,764
[Tonet] Sorry, sorry.

229
00:11:21,847 --> 00:11:23,391
Janine!

230
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:25,309
Janine. Where is that child?

231
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:26,560
So-sorry.

232
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,438
That kid is really stubborn.

233
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:33,109
Janine!

234
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:37,071
[music fades]

235
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:40,991
Hey! Ibyang!

236
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:44,370
Oh? Brother Emerson!

237
00:11:44,453 --> 00:11:47,915
What are you doing here?
You're too young to be wandering around.

238
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:51,210
Uh, I'm with Tatoy and Janine.

239
00:11:51,293 --> 00:11:53,379
- Ah.
- We were going to watch a movie,

240
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:54,922
but I got left behind.

241
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:57,049
- [Emerson] Oh?
- I asked the ticket seller.

242
00:11:57,133 --> 00:12:00,344
They said they didn't go inside.

243
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:02,721
Oh, so where did they go?

244
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:05,474
I'm looking for them too.

245
00:12:06,725 --> 00:12:09,145
Ah. Let's call Atoy.

246
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:11,814
He left his phone at the shop.

247
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,900
Is that so?

248
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:16,402
[suspicious music playing]

249
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,695
Oh, uh, mmm.

250
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:19,280
All right, let's go.

251
00:12:19,363 --> 00:12:20,823
- Let's look for them.
- Okay.

252
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,032
[Emerson] Mmm.

253
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:27,079
[music fades]

254
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,581
- [soft rock music playing]
- Psst. Is it delicious?

255
00:12:28,664 --> 00:12:30,207
This looks delicious. This is delicious.

256
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:31,750
Hold it. Bring it here.

257
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:32,793
Ah! Psst! Psst.

258
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:35,337
Ah… No, no.

259
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:38,257
- [man] Bro, selfie…
- Oh, let's take a selfie.

260
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:39,383
Oh, se-sel…

261
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,051
[lively chatter]

262
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:42,928
There. That's a good one. A good shot.

263
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,638
- [lively chatter]
- [camera shutter snaps]

264
00:12:44,722 --> 00:12:47,057
[teenagers cheer]

265
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:48,225
You're cool, bro!

266
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:54,523
[ominous music playing]

267
00:12:56,775 --> 00:12:58,068
- Atoy!
- [dramatic sting]

268
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,029
Atoy!

269
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:03,282
- Where are you going?
- You followed me?

270
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:04,992
Yes.

271
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:06,160
[foreboding music playing]

272
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:07,620
So come with me…

273
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:10,164
unless you want me to put
a bullet through you.

274
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:15,419
Come on. Let's have a date.

275
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:16,337
‪[dramatic stinging]

276
00:13:25,554 --> 00:13:26,805
[Red] Just walk normally.

277
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:28,641
- [dramatic sting]
- I was right.

278
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:31,393
Janine is a fake child,
and you and Martina know it.

279
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:33,395
You wouldn't do this to me if I was wrong.

280
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:35,814
- Shut up.
- [tense music playing]

281
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:39,985
Why did you have to use another child
to pretend she's her daughter, huh?

282
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,237
What did you do-- [grunts]

283
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:43,822
Psst! I said shut up! Huh?

284
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:45,824
Even if you escape from me here,

285
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:47,910
I'll find you.

286
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:50,538
I'll still kill you.
I'll kill your whole family too.

287
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:51,747
Do you understand?

288
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:52,623
‪-[dramatic sting]
‪-[gasps]

289
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:53,958
- Come on!
- [dramatic sting]

290
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:59,922
Let's just page Atoy at the mall office.
He's probably looking for you too.

291
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:02,258
Where's the office?

292
00:14:02,925 --> 00:14:04,760
I don't know. Let's just find it.

293
00:14:04,843 --> 00:14:05,844
[pensive music playing]

294
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,137
- [thumps]
- Hey!

295
00:14:07,721 --> 00:14:08,889
Are you okay? Hey!

296
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:10,432
Why? What's wrong?

297
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:14,019
You weren't looking!
You bumped into the kid!

298
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:16,021
Be thankful I have work.

299
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:17,898
If not, I'd beat you up.

300
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:19,692
Oh, better get to work then!

301
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:21,944
He thinks we're scared of him?

302
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:23,237
[chuckles]

303
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:25,447
Go to work, or you'll be late!

304
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:31,537
- [exhales]
- Brother Emerson, stop fighting!

305
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,705
Let's go!

306
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:36,208
Why did you stop me just now?
I almost got hit by him.

307
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:37,918
You should've told me earlier.

308
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:39,587
You weren't looking.

309
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:41,505
[chuckles]

310
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,300
[music fades]

311
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,801
[line rings]

312
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:48,554
Martina, tell Roger.

313
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:52,558
I'm with Tonet.
Let's go to the parking lot, okay?

314
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:55,227
Come on.

315
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,770
[rousing music playing]

316
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:58,230
[quivering breath]

317
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:00,774
[gasping and panicking]

318
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:03,569
- [Red] Don't touch her, don't touch her!
- [woman, indistinct]

319
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:05,362
- [Red] Leave her! Leave her!
- [woman] What are you doing?

320
00:15:05,446 --> 00:15:06,280
[Red] Leave her! No, no!

321
00:15:06,363 --> 00:15:07,615
Hands off, hands off!

322
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:10,409
Ah, I-- I'll take her.
I'll bring her to the hospital.

323
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:11,911
[music fades]

324
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,162
- [Atoy] Ibyang!
- There she is!

325
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:14,830
[Emerson] Finally!

326
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:18,250
- Oh my!
- What's wrong with you?

327
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:19,919
Where did you go? Hmm?

328
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:22,463
We've been looking for you!

329
00:15:22,546 --> 00:15:23,797
Hmm?

330
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:26,300
We didn't get to watch the movie.

331
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:27,676
So annoying.

332
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,929
I just tied my shoelace.

333
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:32,556
Then suddenly, you were gone.

334
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:35,809
Good thing Brother Emerson was here.

335
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:40,147
- Bro, thanks.
- [in English] Okay, no prob!

336
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:41,774
But I'll go ahead, bro,

337
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:44,443
because I have a lechon date with Tonet.

338
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:46,987
- [smirks]
- Lechon?

339
00:15:47,071 --> 00:15:48,739
- Really, huh? Lechon?
- Yes!

340
00:15:48,822 --> 00:15:53,035
Because it has sentimental value for us.

341
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:54,828
Since we were kids in Cebu.

342
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:56,664
Even though there's plenty there,

343
00:15:56,747 --> 00:15:58,415
I couldn't afford it.

344
00:15:58,499 --> 00:15:59,917
So, I promised her,

345
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,420
when I become successful,

346
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:06,548
I'd treat her to lechon,
and today's that day.

347
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:11,679
It's a bit pricey
at the restaurant I reserved.

348
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:15,432
But luckily, I have…

349
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:17,267
a discount voucher!

350
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:19,812
[giggles]

351
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:23,107
If you're successful,
why do you still need a voucher?

352
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:25,818
Doesn't using a voucher mean
you have no money?

353
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:27,486
If you have no money,
you're not successful.

354
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:28,696
That's common sense.

355
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:30,739
Mmm… [giggles]

356
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:33,325
You're really cute!

357
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:38,914
Money isn't the only measure of success.

358
00:16:39,456 --> 00:16:41,583
Hmm? Okay? Remember that.

359
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,586
[mellow music playing]

360
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:47,256
[Emerson mutters]

361
00:16:47,756 --> 00:16:48,716
So?

362
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:49,925
Oh, Atoy-- Ouch.

363
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:51,719
- Hey.
- Ouch, ouch!

364
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:53,429
What was that?

365
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:55,723
What-- Hey!

366
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:57,057
- [soft rock music playing]
- [Emerson groans]

367
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:58,642
Wait, wait, wait. Ouch, it hurts.

368
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:01,186
- Stop that thief!
- [Emerson] Huh?

369
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,438
[guard] There's a thief!

370
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:03,897
- A th-thief?
- He's a thief!

371
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:04,898
A thief?

372
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,358
Wait, my wallet?

373
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:08,235
- [guard] Chase him, chase him.
- [gasps]

374
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:10,029
My wallet was stolen, Atoy.

375
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,071
Chase him!

376
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,948
- Retrieve my wallet!
- Huh? Why me?

377
00:17:13,032 --> 00:17:16,535
It can't be Ibyang! Go on. It's there--

378
00:17:16,618 --> 00:17:18,787
- Our voucher's in there!
- Okay, okay! The kids!

379
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:21,457
I'll handle it!
Our lechon voucher is in there!

380
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:22,499
[sighs]

381
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:25,002
Come on? Come on, stop it. Stand up!

382
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:28,839
[soft rock music playing]

383
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,176
Ah, sir, sir, sir!

384
00:17:32,259 --> 00:17:33,302
[Tonet gasping]

385
00:17:33,385 --> 00:17:36,263
Help me! That's a bad man!
He wants to kill me!

386
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:38,223
No-- Gun? He has a gun hidden behind him!

387
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:41,518
No! I don't have a gun!
What are you saying? I don't have a gun!

388
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:43,854
[gasps] Sir, he's lying!

389
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:44,855
Help me!

390
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:46,273
Wait, uh, ma--

391
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:49,943
Sir, she's the one who pretended
to be sick earlier?

392
00:17:50,027 --> 00:17:52,071
Then I'm the bad one?
She's probably the bad one, right?

393
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,739
[woman] This woman was just pretending.

394
00:17:53,822 --> 00:17:54,865
Uh, I think she's a thief!

395
00:17:54,948 --> 00:17:57,785
Now she's just pretending
to be sick to escape.

396
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,453
Huh? I didn't do anything.

397
00:17:59,536 --> 00:18:00,370
Really, I didn't…

398
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,539
[Red] Come here! She's the bad person!

399
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:04,291
[Tonet] He's the bad one!

400
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:05,501
- Not me. Not--
- [Tonet] Don't--

401
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:07,920
- [guard] What happened here?
- No, no. Uh…

402
00:18:08,003 --> 00:18:09,963
Uh, she's a thief. A thief.

403
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:12,925
Pretending to be sick, to evade me!

404
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:14,510
[woman 1] So, you're a thief, miss!

405
00:18:14,593 --> 00:18:16,428
- Yes!
- Are you part of a gang?

406
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:17,679
[tense music playing]

407
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,098
[man] Move aside!

408
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:24,103
[soft rock music playing]

409
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:25,521
[man] Oh, move!

410
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:30,400
[music swells]

411
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:34,279
My fall was terrible. Ouch, ouch.

412
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:35,781
[groans]

413
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:38,158
My day is even worse.

414
00:18:39,076 --> 00:18:40,828
I'm exhausted from walking around.

415
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:42,830
It was supposed
to be bonding time with Daddy,

416
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:44,581
but we ended up everywhere.

417
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:46,291
Oh my.

418
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,335
So annoying.

419
00:18:48,418 --> 00:18:49,837
[scoffs]

420
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:50,754
You know, you…

421
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:54,925
You complain all the time.

422
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:57,719
That attitude isn't good, young girl.

423
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:01,181
It should've been just Daddy and me.

424
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:05,769
Sorry if your day got ruined
because of me.

425
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:09,690
But Tatoy said the three of us
should be together.

426
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:11,567
[pensive music playing]

427
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:13,569
Let it go, let it go.

428
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:15,821
I won't give her any lechon.

429
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:17,156
She won't get any lechon from me.

430
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:19,908
It hurts.

431
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,785
[sighs]

432
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:25,747
Brother Emerson, maybe
you should go to the clinic?

433
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:28,041
You might have a fracture.

434
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,043
No, it's fine. I can handle it.

435
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:33,005
Good thing this happened to me.

436
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:37,009
Maybe this is the third misfortune
the old woman told me about earlier.

437
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:39,303
At least it happened to me.

438
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,930
Not to Tonet.

439
00:19:42,931 --> 00:19:45,517
Why me? Sir, he's the bad person!

440
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:46,518
Sir, not me!

441
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,603
[Tonet] Why me?

442
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:49,188
- He's the bad person!
- Arrest that woman!

443
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:50,731
She stole my cellphone!

444
00:19:50,814 --> 00:19:51,982
- See?
- [guard] Come here!

445
00:19:52,065 --> 00:19:53,358
I'm not a thief!

446
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:54,443
- They're a couple!
- Come on!

447
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:55,611
They're just framing me!

448
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:58,030
- They want to kill me--
- [Red] Sir, no-- No--

449
00:19:58,113 --> 00:20:00,157
We're not a couple. We're just concerned.

450
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,992
It would be better, sir, um…

451
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:03,744
if we take her. We'll take care of her.

452
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:05,120
She should be with the police.

453
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:06,788
- Right?
- Let's go, let's go!

454
00:20:06,872 --> 00:20:07,831
- [Tonet shrieks]
- [guard gasps]

455
00:20:07,915 --> 00:20:08,916
[tense music playing]

456
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:10,083
You're too slow!

457
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:17,299
[music swells]

458
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:22,304
[action music playing]

459
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:30,896
[gasping]

460
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:32,272
[Tonet, in English] Excuse me.

461
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:35,317
[Tonet gasping]

462
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:37,486
- [Tonet squealing]
- [clamoring]

463
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:39,947
[Tonet shrieks]

464
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,281
[screaming]

465
00:20:44,743 --> 00:20:45,994
[gasps]

466
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:51,625
[soft rock music playing]

467
00:20:58,465 --> 00:20:59,758
[Red] Move aside!

468
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:01,635
Move aside. Move aside!

469
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:04,096
Get out of the way!

470
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:05,472
Where are you going?

471
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:10,602
[dramatic stinging]

472
00:21:11,186 --> 00:21:13,230
- [Red] Hey! Where are you going?
- [guard shouts]

473
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,198
- [music fades]
- [panting]

474
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:27,619
‪[dramatic stinging]

475
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,498
[Atoy] You bastard.

476
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:32,958
You really made me chase you.

477
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:34,960
Give me my friend's wallet.

478
00:21:35,043 --> 00:21:36,962
[pants]

479
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:38,255
This wallet?

480
00:21:39,047 --> 00:21:40,090
Give it.

481
00:21:42,175 --> 00:21:44,344
So, this is all of it? This wallet!

482
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:46,888
Here, take it!

483
00:21:49,474 --> 00:21:50,559
Son of a--

484
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:54,062
Keep the money. The voucher.

485
00:21:54,688 --> 00:21:57,107
I need the voucher. It's important to him.
Give it back.

486
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:58,650
This?

487
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,193
You have to take it from me.

488
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:02,487
I'm not giving it back
without something in return.

489
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:04,656
[music fades]

490
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:05,741
Maybe you got something for me?

491
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:08,660
- Like what?
- Anything, in exchange for this.

492
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:10,037
The money isn't enough.

493
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:13,040
[tense music playing]

494
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:22,299
Give me your wallet instead.

495
00:22:22,382 --> 00:22:24,760
Your friend's money isn't enough.

496
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,011
Right, boys?

497
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:28,221
- [teenagers] Yes, it's not enough!
- Not at all!

498
00:22:28,305 --> 00:22:31,224
[dramatic sting]

499
00:22:31,308 --> 00:22:32,934
[car door clicks shut]

500
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:37,481
Uh, bros…

501
00:22:38,231 --> 00:22:40,901
Uh, calm down.

502
00:22:40,984 --> 00:22:42,110
Calm down and relax.

503
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:44,404
All I'm asking for is that voucher.

504
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:46,698
Huh? The voucher is all I want.

505
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:48,700
You can have the money.

506
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:50,243
Give me your wallet first.

507
00:22:50,327 --> 00:22:52,370
- My wallet?
- Yes. In exchange for this.

508
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:54,706
[ominous music playing]

509
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:56,750
Right, boys? The money
isn't enough for us!

510
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,335
[teenagers] Yes!

511
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:00,337
Relax. Okay, okay, wait.

512
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:02,881
Just give me that. And I'll give you this.

513
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:05,550
This? Okay.

514
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:08,261
- We'll exchange, huh.
- [music fades]

515
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:09,763
[grunting and groaning]

516
00:23:09,846 --> 00:23:11,181
- [thumping]
- [grunting]

517
00:23:12,307 --> 00:23:13,934
- [weapons swooshing]
- [grunting and groaning]

518
00:23:14,017 --> 00:23:15,602
[thumping]

519
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:25,112
[music fades]

520
00:23:26,988 --> 00:23:29,658
[panting]

521
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:31,326
Oh, Lord. Thank you, Lord.

522
00:23:31,409 --> 00:23:33,870
Good thing I escaped. [panting]

523
00:23:33,954 --> 00:23:35,872
[panting]

524
00:23:41,461 --> 00:23:43,547
[ominous music playing]

525
00:23:47,467 --> 00:23:50,178
[panting]

526
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:52,305
Oh, thank you, Lord. I escaped.

527
00:23:52,389 --> 00:23:55,892
[panting continues]

528
00:23:55,976 --> 00:23:57,018
[Martina, in English]
That's what you think.

529
00:23:58,562 --> 00:24:02,315
[rousing music playing]

530
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:13,618
[electronic blipping]

531
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:22,252
Leave me alone!
I already have a quiet life!

532
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:24,546
- [clangs]
- [grunting]

533
00:24:24,629 --> 00:24:26,965
UP NEXT

534
00:24:27,048 --> 00:24:28,633
[clangs]

535
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:30,760
- [clinks]
- What is that?

536
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:35,599
[Atoy] <i>This belongs to Tonet.</i>

537
00:24:37,184 --> 00:24:38,393
Have you seen Tonet?

538
00:24:38,476 --> 00:24:39,978
Atoy beat me to it.

539
00:24:40,061 --> 00:24:41,563
[Atoy] <i>Let's get out of here.</i>
<i>This place looks dangerous.</i>

540
00:24:41,646 --> 00:24:44,691
[Ibyang] Tatoy, something's moving…

541
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:46,151
Maybe a kitten!

542
00:24:46,234 --> 00:24:47,485
<i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

543
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:49,946
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

544
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:52,866
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

545
00:24:52,949 --> 00:24:54,492
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

546
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:55,911
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
